6. findIndex() in JavaScript

The findIndex() method returns the index of the first element in an array that satisfies a condition.

Syntax
array.findIndex(callback);

Example 1: Find the index of a number
const numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40];

const index = numbers.findIndex(num => num > 25);

console.log(index); // 2

const users = [
  { id: 1, name: "John" },
  { id: 2, name: "Alice" }
];

const index = users.findIndex(user => user.id === 2);

if (index !== -1) {
  users[index].name = "Alex";
}

console.log(users);


Easy way to remember:

find() → give me the element
findIndex() → give me the element's index
If no match: find() → undefined, findIndex() → -1


